  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5090",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological activity of LOUCY through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging from the interaction between Mollicellin N and P2X purinoceptors. This pathway involves Mollicellin N targeting P2X purinoceptor 1 and P2X purinoceptor 7, both of which are known receptors for extracellular nucleotides. These receptors are involved in cellular signaling processes, and their modulation by Mollicellin N suggests a potential role in modulating intracellular signaling cascades. The second pathway, involving [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, also leads to LOUCY as a target, indicating that the compound may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by inhibiting the same or related purinoceptors. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Mollicellin N to LOUCY highlights the complexity of the interaction network, but the shared involvement of purinoceptors suggests a common biological mechanism. The evidence supports a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating purinoceptor activity, which could have implications for therapeutic applications targeting these receptors.",
